      "worked": "For $x>0$, the product law gives\n$$\\begin{align*}g(x)&=\\ln2+\\ln x\\\\g(x)&=\\ln2+f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\ln2$ is constant,\n$$\\begin{align*}g'(x)&=0+f'(x)\\\\g'(x)&=f'(x).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
